WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:05.211
Hey Youtubers it’s Charlie and since it’s
been a while since I’ve done a new Doctor

00:00:05.211 --> 00:00:10.570
Who video and there was a Horror Channel special
coming on April 18th, I wanted to do my Top

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.429
10 favorite scary episodes of Classic Who.

00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:17.970
The horror channel is airing a bunch of scary
episodes as part of a special, but they’re

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:22.859
also all available on the web on either Netflix
or Hulu.

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:29.619
Also quick heads up, I have to go to Las Vegas
for my brother’s Bachelor Party this weekend.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:37.090
I’ll be back in time to do all my Sunday
Game of Thrones videos, but if I do a Saturday

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.340
video it will probably be on my laptop camera
or iphone.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.340
So early warning in case it looks weird.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.990
Before we get started with my list in case
you didn’t see, there have been a few more

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:46.800
villain cast in series 8 including Ben Miller
and Keeley Hawes.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.770
We don’t know if they’ll only appear in
one episode or multiple yet.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.820
But they are most definitely evil.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:56.640
We can talk more about them in a future bonus
video.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.539
So let’s talk scary Classic Who.

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:01.510
Most of which was inspired by really scary
classic sci fi book stories.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:05.660
Feel free to add your own favorites as we
go along but here we go.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.760
Number 10 - Deadly Assassin.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.650
The image most people associate with this
episode is the husk form Master, nightmare

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.550
inducing all by itself.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.430
But the episode inovked this really big plot
to siphon off regeneration energy from the

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:23.190
Eye of Harmony and this Manchurian Candidate
Presidential race.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.030
Just in general a really good meta mashup
of other really awesome stories.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.141
Here’s a list of some of the other shows
and movies that they paid homage to in the

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:31.220
episode.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:36.610
North By Northwest, awesome Hitchcock movie,
Sherlock Holmes and The Empty House and a

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.220
couple of Star Trek Original Series episodes
like The Arena and Shore Leave.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.860
Supposedly it was also the only Classic Who
episode to not feature a companion.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.720
Number 9 - Robots of Death.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.680
The robots in this story reminded me a little
of the Clockwork robots in Girl in the Fireplace.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.490
A human basically gets raised by robots and
eventually thinks of them as superior.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.860
Not only do they look super creepy, there’s
this really horrible moment when The Doctor

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.880
gets stuck inside a storage room that’s
slowly filling with Sand.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.560
This episode was inspired by some of my favorite
classic sci fi stories like Frank Herbert’s

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.840
Dune, because Sandminers, Isaac Asimov’s
I Robot.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.489
Not the terrible Will Smith version either.

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:15.579
The original and Arthur C. Clarke’s Fall
of Moondust.

00:02:15.579 --> 00:02:18.310
I did think it was pretty funny the villain
was killed because helium made his voice all

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.310
weird.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:22.870
But it is pretty scary to think robots you’ve
been worshipping you’re whole life end up

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:23.870
killing you.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.569
I guess that might scare you off of ever having
children too.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:28.019
Number 8 - Pyramids of Mars

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:29.849
A great Sutekh episode.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:34.499
I saw a couple of you guys wanted to see the
character brought back eventually.

00:02:34.499 --> 00:02:39.430
But there’s this really awesome line where
Sutekh says You’re evil is my good.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.859
I am Sutekh the destroyer.

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:44.569
Where I tread, I leave nothing but dust and
darkness.

00:02:44.569 --> 00:02:48.069
Because it’s a mummy story there’s a lot
of mythological influences like the classic

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:54.090
Hammer Mummy films, H.G. Wells, Norse Mythology,
Loki in prison shout out and Bram Stoker’s

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.090
Jewel of the Seven Stars.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:03:01.280
One of my favorite parts about classic episodes
like this are that because special effects

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.000
and action were so much harder to do, they
had to rely on amazing dialogue.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.840
Thus you get these crazy awesome Sutekh speeches.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.459
One of the best bad guys ever.

00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:12.470
It also involves more evil robots.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.849
I feel like Doctor Who is always trying to
tell us not to trust robots.

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:21.250
Other than K-9 let me know which robots you
think we can trust in the doctor who universe.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.770
The teselecta is kind of a robot ship.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.969
But it’s operated by people.

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:26.790
It’s not self aware.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.580
Number 7 - Terror Of The Zygons.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.450
If you didn’t know them from Tom Baker’s
run, then you’ll definitely know them from

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.170
the 50th Anniversary.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:38.750
Since they’re shape shifters I always think
of Invasion of the Body Snatchers.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.299
Which is another great horror sci fi story.

00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:44.719
The episode was also inspired by The Private
life of Sherlock Holmes.

00:03:44.719 --> 00:03:47.830
I always love it when Sherlock and Doctor
Who crossover.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:51.549
If you haven’t seen this episode before,
watch it, then watch the 50th Anniversary

00:03:51.549 --> 00:03:52.549
again.

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:55.859
There’s a lot of callbacks during the special
that make it a lot more fun when you’ve

00:03:55.859 --> 00:03:57.849
seen the older story.

00:03:57.849 --> 00:03:59.370
Number 6 - Tomb Of The Cybermen.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:04.060
One of my few Second Doctor stories on this
list, but another egyptian mythology, mummy

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.060
story.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:06.060
I’m sensing another pattern.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.989
Don’t trust robots, don’t trust pyramids.

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:09.969
And maybe riddles too.

00:04:09.969 --> 00:04:13.939
What is it about uncovering ancient knowledge
that always makes things go so horribly wrong.

00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:17.810
A scientist just want to learn a little bit
about the Cybermen and all the crazies come

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.250
out of the woodwork to join the expedition.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.346
I guess in situations like this you would
really just complain to you’re human resources

00:04:20.346 --> 00:04:21.346
officer for hiring such sketching people to
join your team.

00:04:21.346 --> 00:04:23.650
If you want to get really meta, you should
check out The Curse of The Mummy’s Tomb.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.150
It was the primary inspiration for this episode.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:27.930
Number 5 - The Daemons.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.320
Into John Pertwee’s years.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.050
There’s actually a ton of scary stories
during his run.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:37.080
But this one kind of reminds me of the Weeping
Angels and The Beast just visually.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.060
Other big red flags for the Doctor in this
episode.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.660
There’s a town called Devil’s End.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.910
The Master gets involved with Black Magic
and tries to take these demonic powers.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:50.060
The character Azal was actually really interesting
and tragic.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.740
I don’t know how they’d bring him back,
just based on the way the episode ended.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:57.610
But he really stands out as one of the better
classic who monsters.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:01.940
Here’s a couple other stories that inspired
the episode.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:06.390
Village of the Damned, Star Trek Who Mourn’s
For Adonis and there’s even another Sherlock

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:07.390
shout out.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.370
Elementary my dear Benton.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.820
Number 4 - Genesis Of The Daleks.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:15.560
Early Tom Baker meets Davros, you can’t
go wrong.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.960
A really awesome Skaro based episode in case
you’ve never seen the homeworld of the Daleks.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.060
I feel like most people today just associate
the Daleks with their current form.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:28.600
But in this episode you learn about the humanoid
race they descended from.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.520
Or evolved from, depending on how you look
at it.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:39.110
It’s also another one of those stories,
where an evil scientist is killed by his creation.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.250
It really reminds me of Frankenstein.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.720
Only there’s like millions of monsters running
around instead of just one monster.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.660
Here’s a big question, if Classic Who had
ever done a straight up Bride of The Daleks

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.085
story just to push the Frankestein mythos
further.

00:05:47.085 --> 00:05:49.010
What would have played the role of the monster
Bride.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:52.220
Like an Elsa Lanchester Dalek or something?

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.470
Number 3 - Terror Of The Autons.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.820
Another great Unit story that was also a Master
story.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:02.400
And it also involves a Bomb inside UNIT headquarters,
just like the 50th Anniversary.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.550
You know how some people are afraid of clowns.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:09.460
Well this really gives circuses a bad name
too.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:14.540
I did love how the Doctor and The Master were
forced to work together for a little while.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:18.260
There’s something so interesting about enemies
forgetting their enemies for a little while.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:23.770
So big takeaways from this episode are don’t
trust Carnivale folk and robots are still

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.670
evil.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:35.010
There was even a later John Pertwee episode
called Carnivale of Monsters.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.820
Number 2 - The Curse of Fenric.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:41.700
My only seventh Doctor story but a really
awesome mashup of a zombie story and a vampire

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:42.700
story.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:46.580
It ends up turning into this classic situation
where scientists get to clever and a super

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:50.540
computer they design let’s ancient evil
loose making everything go crazy.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.850
I think that’s why the Doctor always tells
people not to touch buttons when they’re

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:54.960
in the TARDIS.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:00.120
Something always goes wrong when you turn
on mysterious machines or read ancient runes.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.120
Lesson learned.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:09.550
If you ever wake up in a Doctor Who story,
just don’t touch or read anything.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:14.670
And my number one favorite Scary Classic Who
episode - Caves of Androzani.

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:18.620
Just one of the best episodes of Classic Who
in general, but every time I see Jek I think

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.920
about Scorpius from Farscape.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:25.160
Just visually so scary to look at, and on
top of that, Jek is this really put upon tragic

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:31.260
villain who forces the Doctor to sacrifice
himself to save his companion.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:36.180
It was the final Peter Davison episode and
featured his regeneration into Colin Baker’s

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.340
Sixth Doctor.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:38.340
So now it’s you’re turn.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:41.270
Let me know what your favorite scary episode
of Doctor Who is.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.900
It doesn’t have to be a classic episode.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.050
Just one that you think is really really scary.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:50.690
Like I said, I’m out of town on Saturday,
I might post a bonus video using my iphone

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:51.760
just for fun.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:56.250
But I’ll be instagramming the shit out of
Las Vegas.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:02.020
So you can folllow me there or on Twitter
for fun stuff.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:06.230
Right now you can click here to learn more
about The Master coming back for series 8

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.700
and click here to learn more about Danny Pink,
the new character.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.720
Thanks for watching, see you guys this weekend.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:11.139
High Fives!

